SYNTHESIS
  Data-circuit lesson: low Walsh degree or a one-literal threshold is a
  compressed computation, not a proof route, unless it supplies the
  proof-circuit inputs demanded by the certificate DAG.
  The most frequent missing inputs are the real bottlenecks above.
  Therefore the next LRC14 ledger should store proof_circuit_missing_input_vector
  beside root/ear, finite-address, observer-gluing, cocycle, and endpoint-owner fields.
